![](/weird-guys.png "A picture of a woman holding some birds in her hand up for inspection. She is not impressed.")

This is a list of weird little guys in the free software movement and adjacent
spaces. Request additions, removals, or changes [via
email](mailto:drew@ddevault.org); patches welcome.

**Don't harass these people!** Don't engage with them at all.

[An RSS feed for this page is available]($link.page('weird-guys').alternative('rss')).

Artwork by [@p@hj.9fs.net](https://hj.9fs.net/p)

# [FAQ]($heading.id("faq"))

**What is the criteria for being on this list?**

1. Weird, public politics, as judged by yours truly
2. Leader in their community or otherwise powerful/influential
3. Involved in free and open source software

**But that guy does good work!**

A lot of people on this list have done good work. A lot of people not on this
list have done good work, too.

**Will you write a "cool people" list, too?**

No. Who's on the list or off the list will introduce weird social dynamics, and
risks creating a kind of popularity contest. Also, if I published a list like
that, it would paint a target on the backs of everyone on the list for
harassment or worse.

